  "interpretation": "A counted 24-weight local impulse-response predictor can learn the self-generated echo from randomized outgoing-command copies without reading the material matrix. Once learned, it suppresses self-query writing by orders of magnitude. After a valid material change, a fast echo predictor re-tracks the new response before much false structural writing accumulates, whereas a frozen/slow predictor corrupts more. However, persistent temporally correlated prediction error still writes the material even when no external event occurred. Exact Gate-6 cancellation was therefore an ideal benchmark, not a solved mechanism."
